Remove `boot.bootspec.enable = true` from the lanzaboote module.

nixpkgs turned `boot.bootspec.enable` into a mkRemovedOptionModule (bootspec is
now always generated), so any definition of it aborts evaluation. lanzaboote
v1.0.0 still sets it; upstream dropped the line post-1.0.0 in commit
0403b4b7e8b2612657f0053a4c315e6c43eee9e6 but has not cut a tagged release.

--- a/nix/modules/lanzaboote.nix
+++ b/nix/modules/lanzaboote.nix
@@ -240,7 +240,6 @@
     ];

     boot.bootspec = {
-      enable = true;
       extensions."org.nix-community.lanzaboote" = {
         sort_key = config.boot.lanzaboote.sortKey;
       };
